course: dictionary
lesson: 10891
title: VIP: a short word with a big meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: VIP is a short way of writing «very important person». Each letter stands for a word, so VIP is an abbreviation. It is written in capitals, and you can add an s to make VIPs for more than one person.
explain: A VIP is someone famous or important who gets special treatment, such as a celebrity, a leader or an honoured guest. VIP can also describe things made for those people, like VIP seats, a VIP lounge or a VIP pass.
explain: «So they piled cushions on the floor and called it the VIP section, and suddenly everyone wanted it.» The floor did not change, but the name did. The name VIP tells you the section is meant for special people, and that is why everyone wanted it.
explain: «How you name a place, like calling the floor the VIP section, can change how it feels to sit there.» A name can make a place feel special. When you meet an unknown short word, look for its full form and the clues around it.
fact: VIP is an abbreviation of «very important person».
fact: A VIP is someone famous or important who gets special treatment.
fact: «VIP» can also describe things, such as VIP seats, a VIP lounge or a VIP pass.
fact: Examples of VIPs include celebrities, leaders and honoured guests.
fact: Abbreviations are shortened words, and VIP is usually written in capital letters.
exercise: What does VIP stand for? | Very inspired poet | Very invited pupil | Very interesting person | *Very important person
exercise: What is a VIP? | A person who is always late | A ticket that costs the least | *A famous or important person who gets special treatment | A type of cushion
exercise: Find and copy the short word that stands for «very important person». | floor | *VIP | section | cushions
test: In «calling the floor the VIP section», what does the name change? | *How the place feels to sit in | The number of cushions | The colour of the floor | The height of the ceiling
test: The sign said «VIP lounge». Who is it most likely for? | Passing dogs | Children on a school trip | Rubbish collectors | *Important or special guests
exam: Why is VIP called an abbreviation? | *Because it is a shortened form of «very important person» | Because it rhymes with another word | Because it is a long word | Because it is always written in lower case
